1
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,740
It's the Monster Chief!

2
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,740
Alright, if it's come to this,

3
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:19,400
Yah!

4
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:31,380
Come on, Monster Chief,
disturber of the peace!

5
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:44,720
Same old pattern every time,

6
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,760
N-no, no, kana, kanaa...

7
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:48,640
Four, four!

8
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:56,640
So you've shown up, Monster Chief!

9
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:59,420
Hey, how long are you
going to keep dozing off?

10
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:01,400
Whoa, Chief!

11
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:03,140
You idiot!

12
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:11,200
When you watch TV, brighten the
room and sit farther back, okay?

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,340
Anyone who's broke, come to my place.

14
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:29,060
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

15
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:36,380
Look at the blue sky, the white clouds.

16
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:42,800
It'll all work out eventually.

17
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,040
You get it, right?

18
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:48,000
Got it, got it.

19
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Once you get it, quietly follow me!

20
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:08,400
Onrei Katsushika Pro Wrestling

21
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:17,160
Great. I never expected the
real thing to show up there.

22
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:22,680
Even if told to get to work,
the world is perfectly peaceful.

23
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:32,080
Katsushika Pro Wrestling?

24
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,920
Never heard of that group.

25
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:37,780
Guess we'll watch for a bit.

26
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:38,940
Hey, hold on.

27
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:49,500
What's with this old-fashioned wrestling?

28
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:07,060
With this many empty seats,

29
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,620
you should do this somewhere else.

30
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:10,700
What?!

31
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:15,420
This wrestling is so outdated,

32
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:17,860
like it's from a previous era.

33
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,660
Found you! You there!

34
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:27,320
Me?

35
00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:30,900
Yes, you! Won't you step into our ring?

36
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:31,760
What?

37
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:41,348
Actually,
I've been keeping this a secret until now,

38
00:03:41,398 --> 00:03:44,397
but Katsushika Pro Wrestling
has been running in the red,

39
00:03:44,447 --> 00:03:47,700
and at this rate,
the group's survival is in danger.

40
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:51,060
Secret? Anyone can see that just by looking!

41
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:52,180
Th-that's true.

42
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:55,380
Ever since I was a child,
I've loved pro wrestling,

43
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:57,300
and last year I quit my salaryman job

44
00:03:57,720 --> 00:04:01,220
and finally founded my
long-dreamed-of wrestling group.

45
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:04,680
Somehow,
attendance just isn't growing at all.

46
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:05,940
I suppose so.

47
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:08,740
Nobody would want to watch that.

48
00:04:08,740 --> 00:04:09,680
Why is that?

49
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:13,240
I'm working so hard, though.

50
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:15,000
Why, why?

51
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,060
First of all,
pro wrestling itself is outdated.

52
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:21,360
That's the same as the wrestling from Rikidozan's day,
isn't it?

53
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:25,400
But the wrestling I loved
was that kind of thing...

54
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,600
That's the problem.

55
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:29,220
The fighting world evolves every day.

56
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:32,520
Your wrestling is clearly behind the times.

57
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:35,380
Then what should I do?

58
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:37,160
Well, let's see.

59
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:41,040
Alright, leave everything to me!

60
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,480
W-well then,

61
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:48,120
then I'll become the wrestler and producer
and revive this organization myself.

62
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,400
Really?

63
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:53,780
But half the profits are mine, got it?

64
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:55,800
Pro wrestling...

65
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:59,700
Yeah, I want you all to lend a hand too.

66
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:02,860
Why would we have to do pro wrestling?

67
00:05:03,260 --> 00:05:04,580
No way, not that.

68
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:06,680
Yeah, I'm not really into that either.

69
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,443
How pathetic.

70
00:05:08,493 --> 00:05:12,120
So you two are really that cold-hearted?

71
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,640
It's so pitiful,
it's bringing tears to my eyes.

72
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:17,560
S-senpai...

73
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:18,560
Ryo-chan.

74
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:22,080
Once upon a time, there was a man.

75
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:26,700
He loved pro wrestling more than anyone.

76
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:29,266
Then one day, to make his dream come true,

77
00:05:29,316 --> 00:05:31,620
he founded a pro wrestling group himself.

78
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,700
That was Katsushika Pro Wrestling.

79
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:37,140
But the recession hit hard,
and the business collapsed.

80
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:40,220
They had no choice but to close up shop.

81
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:43,740
But I want to say this:

82
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:46,300
must dreams be given up?

83
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:48,620
No, that's wrong. Absolutely wrong.

84
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:51,740
Dreams must never be abandoned!

85
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:54,620
And yet, and yet...

86
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:57,060
You guys... you guys...

87
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:59,880
What did you become police officers for?

88
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:02,820
Wasn't it to help people in trouble?

89
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:13,100
Let's make the path of a man who staked everything on his dream glorious with our own hands, shall we?
Right, everyone? Senpai, I was wrong.

90
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:17,720
That's admirable, Ryo-chan.
Ryo-san, I'll do my best too!

91
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:21,240
Good, that's exactly why I picked you lot.

92
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,420
Well, well, Kankichi.

93
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:35,520
Ryotsu, what do you think you're doing?

94
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:39,120
Don't you want to fight someone stronger?

95
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:39,980
What?

96
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:44,120
Of course I'll do it.

97
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:48,040
If it's a favor from Ryo-san,
I'll do anything.

98
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,320
I knew you'd say that.

99
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:53,220
Ahhhhhh.

100
00:06:55,800 --> 00:07:01,100
I see, after hearing that, we can't refuse to help.
Well, thanks, that's a relief.

101
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:01,760
Mm.

102
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:03,360
Mm.

103
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:13,480
I'll show you that pro wrestling's home is America.
Looking forward to it.

104
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:22,840
Alright, is everyone here?

105
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:26,740
Then, I'm handing out costumes
and scripts to everyone now.

106
00:07:26,740 --> 00:07:29,220
Make sure you read them
thoroughly before the match.

107
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:30,240
Scripts?

108
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:33,580
Pro wrestling isn't just about the matches.

109
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:36,540
It needs drama leading up to them.

110
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:38,500
The wrestlers' characters

111
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:41,220
and the drama outside
the ring that suits them

112
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:42,820
are absolutely essential.

113
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:45,220
So that's how it is.

114
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:49,700
We have to wear these?

115
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,740
Do I really have to do this?

116
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,240
I knew I wouldn't like it.

117
00:07:53,660 --> 00:07:58,526
Baka-bam! Are you really going
to abandon someone in trouble?

118
00:07:58,576 --> 00:08:01,120
What did you become police officers for?

119
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:03,740
Senpai, I was wrong.

120
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,460
You're admirable, Ryo-chan.

121
00:08:05,940 --> 00:08:08,180
Ryo-san, I'll do my best too.

122
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:11,295
That's the spirit,
you guys I've taken under my wing.

123
00:08:11,345 --> 00:08:12,960
Well, shall we go see?

124
00:08:18,980 --> 00:08:21,020
Ladies and gentlemen gathered at the venue,

125
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:23,660
starting today, Katsushika Pro Wrestling

126
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:27,420
will be reborn as New
Katsushika Pro Wrestling.

127
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,180
And now,

128
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:33,600
Move aside already, you poor bastards!

129
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:39,580
What the hell is that?

130
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:50,340
Nice to meet you,
all you paupers gathered here.

131
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:55,340
I am the owner of Gorgeous Mask
Shin-Katsushika Pro Wrestling.

132
00:08:55,340 --> 00:09:01,680
Today, for paupers like you,
I'll show you the finest wrestling there is.

133
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:05,140
After all, I have money.

134
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:10,540
What's the matter, former owner?

135
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:12,180
Don't hesitate, pick it up.

136
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:14,240
You must be in need of money.

137
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:23,620
Come on, owner, hurry and pick it up.

138
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:26,180
Or do you want more than that?

139
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:29,580
Here you go, how about this?

140
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:32,800
Wait!

141
00:09:34,060 --> 00:09:37,360
Someone who would defile the common people's entertainment,
pro wrestling, with money,

142
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:38,900
I won't stand for it.

143
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:44,320
How unpleasant.
Poor folk have climbed into the ring.

144
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:46,340
Go home at once.

145
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:48,480
Here's your train fare.

146
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:52,680
To money-grubbing wretches like you,

147
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:55,380
I won't let you do as you
please with the sacred ring.

148
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:56,340
Fine.

149
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,560
Then face us in a match.

150
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:00,740
If by some chance you manage to beat us,

151
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:02,680
we'll hand over the ownership to you.

152
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:05,100
I accept that challenge!

153
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:12,180
Red corner, 190 cm, 120 kg.

154
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:15,000
Mad Volbo!

155
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:20,660
Blue corner, 168 cm, 82 kg.

156
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:22,820
Kabutoree Mask!

157
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:26,500
Let's go!

158
00:10:26,760 --> 00:10:28,060
Bring it on, you bastard!

159
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,760
You can't have a match if you can see me,
you idiot!

160
00:10:29,940 --> 00:10:30,760
Shut up and come at me!

161
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:31,760
Where are you going?

162
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:34,840
Where are you going?

163
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:48,560
Aaaaaah!

164
00:10:48,860 --> 00:11:10,900
Uuuuuuuuuuuughhh...

165
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:13,640
What are you doing? It's time for the match!

166
00:11:15,180 --> 00:11:18,960
Forget the match! Look at this!

167
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:21,460
That's company money!

168
00:11:21,460 --> 00:11:26,100
What's going on?
Wasn't he on the owner's side?

169
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:29,000
Money is everything in this world.

170
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,960
Well then, farewell.

171
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:33,900
How awful!

172
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,240
What a bastard!

173
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,060
Get back here! I'll knock you flat!

174
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:39,540
It's too late now.

175
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:42,520
Hyahyahyahya!

176
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:43,060
Hold it!

177
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:54,181
Go for it, Mashikoda Gambler!

178
00:11:54,231 --> 00:11:55,760
This is everyone's money!

179
00:11:57,580 --> 00:12:00,900
Ugh, m-mujin...

180
00:12:00,900 --> 00:12:02,400
*Slump*

181
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:12,620
I've never gotten this much applause before.

182
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:18,240
Everything went exactly
according to the script.

183
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:20,960
Thank you, everyone.

184
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:25,480
Thanks to you, we got great publicity
for Shin-Katsushika Pro Wrestling.

185
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:28,920
We just did what anyone would do.

186
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:32,520
Well, about the next match...

187
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:34,760
The next match?

188
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:40,820
Owner, a customer came by earlier!
Hurry up, go on, go!

189
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:42,240
I see.

190
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:49,260
What do you mean, the next match?

191
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:51,420
Wasn't that the last one?

192
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:55,380
Ryo-san said it would be the owner's grand farewell,
didn't he?

193
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:56,780
Idiots!

194
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:59,720
Today's match is just the first step.

195
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:02,720
Shinkatsu Shika Pro Wrestling
is still just getting started.

196
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:05,580
We're almost able to be reborn, you know.

197
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:07,220
And yet...

198
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:09,780
And yet you guys...

199
00:13:09,780 --> 00:13:11,460
Fine, fine, we get it.

200
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:12,700
I see.

201
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:15,440
Good. I'm glad you understand.

202
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:16,660
Nyahaha!

203
00:13:17,660 --> 00:13:19,100
Aaaaaah!

204
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:19,980
Aaaaaah!

205
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:26,980
Help!

206
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:36,840
Pro wrestling is the best!

207
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:39,380
Morning.

208
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:42,905
Well, setting Ryotsu aside,

209
00:13:42,955 --> 00:13:45,320
Nakagawa and Reiko haven't come in yet?

210
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:46,680
Good morning!

211
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:51,800
S-sorry, we're late.

212
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,120
Well, you're not late yet.

213
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,720
It's rare for everyone to come in together.

214
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,100
Yeah, well...

215
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:02,220
Senpai, this really isn't possible.

216
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:04,500
A nationwide tour while we're working?

217
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:06,020
Don't complain.

218
00:14:06,020 --> 00:14:08,580
We made it in time,
so that's good enough, isn't it?

219
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:12,820
I'm not letting a chance to make
this kind of big money slip away.

220
00:14:12,820 --> 00:14:13,980
Hey, Ryotsu.

221
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:16,660
Yes, what is it?

222
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:22,220
That article...

223
00:14:22,220 --> 00:14:24,460
our match yesterday

224
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:27,620
Apparently there's some
interesting wrestling going on lately

225
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:29,860
Have you ever seen it?

226
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:31,960
This is the first I've heard of it.

227
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:33,680
What about you, Nakagawa?

228
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:34,680
And you, Reiko?

229
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:38,180
No, I didn't know either.

230
00:14:38,740 --> 00:14:40,360
There's such a thing?

231
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:41,660
I didn't know.

232
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:42,600
I see.

233
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:45,040
The chief and everyone at
the station went to see it,

234
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:47,620
and apparently it was quite entertaining.

235
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:52,299
Well,

236
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:55,880
Pro wrestling hasn't been this
big since Rikidozan on the street TV

237
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,180
Senpai, this is bad.

238
00:15:01,180 --> 00:15:03,400
If the Chief finds out...

239
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,980
Don't worry.

240
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:08,440
The Chief didn't find out, so we're fine.

241
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:12,580
But Chief Ohara has pretty good instincts.

242
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:16,020
Th-that's true.

243
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,880
So this is the ticket counter.

244
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:25,460
Excuse me, about the New
Katsushika Pro Wrestling tickets...

245
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:28,360
Sorry, we're all sold out.

246
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,740
All of them?

247
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:36,780
Yes, New Katsushika Pro Wrestling is as popular as a Giants game.
They sell out the moment they go on sale.

248
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,560
It's that big?

249
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:44,720
Phew, that was close.

250
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:46,620
Hello?

251
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:50,580
Excuse me, about the New
Katsushika Pro Wrestling tickets...

252
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:53,980
All tickets for today's sale have sold out.

253
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,480
Not again.

254
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:04,820
The last one.

255
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:16,440
I could've sworn that was silver.

256
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:18,440
Too bad, here's a tissue.

257
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:25,100
This one's no good, that one's no good.
What's going on?

258
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:27,220
Hey there, you.

259
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:32,120
You want to go see the wrestling, don't you?

260
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:34,880
How did you know that?

261
00:16:34,880 --> 00:16:38,220
But you absolutely must
not go see the wrestling.

262
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:38,940
What?

263
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:42,080
If you go, you'll be miserable.

264
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:43,120
Understand?

265
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:46,980
You must never go see the wrestling,
mind you.

266
00:16:47,860 --> 00:16:48,740
N-no way...

267
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:49,020
Hey...

268
00:16:52,820 --> 00:16:56,960
After warning them that much,
even the Chief won't come to watch, right?

269
00:16:56,960 --> 00:17:00,660
Ryo-san,
what are we going to do in the next match?

270
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:05,560
I've already got a plan. Look at this.

271
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:09,440
This is the championship belt!

272
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:13,400
It's a title match in battle royal format,
with all wrestlers taking part.

273
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:17,480
The last one left in
the ring becomes champion.

274
00:17:19,020 --> 00:17:24,800
That's brilliant! Right? Right?
Alright, we'll make the next one flashy too!

275
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:35,180
Good grief! Watching wrestling brings misfortune?
Well, you can't get tickets anyway, so go see it!

276
00:17:35,180 --> 00:17:35,940
But still...

277
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,560
Thank you very much. Here, take this.

278
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:44,000
W-what is this?

279
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:47,640
Hey, what's the meaning of this ticket?

280
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:49,460
Oh, that's...

281
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:52,220
Look, just look over there.

282
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:56,620
Well, apparently the shopping district
chairman was saddled with a whole bunch of them.

283
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:59,220
They're handing them out for free
to anyone who makes a purchase.

284
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:00,720
W-what?

285
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:10,560
Thanks to all of you,
the venue is packed to capacity!

286
00:18:13,740 --> 00:18:14,740
Aaaaaah!

287
00:18:14,740 --> 00:18:16,280
Aaaaaah!

288
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:31,880
And now, the rapidly growing New Katsushika Pro
Wrestling's first-ever dome event of the year!

289
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:35,920
And this time, it's our first title match,
so it's truly a night of firsts!

290
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:39,720
I wonder how they'll entertain us this time.

291
00:18:42,740 --> 00:18:46,680
Welcome,
all you poor folks gathered in this venue.

292
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:57,580
I never expected to get a
ticket in a place like that.

293
00:18:57,580 --> 00:18:59,300
I'm really lucky.

294
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:05,440
Tonight, our New Katsu Underground Pro
Wrestling will hold its first title match.

295
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:08,540
Who is the strongest wrestler, I wonder?

296
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:10,500
Entrance!

297
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,840
I'm taking the belt!

298
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:25,860
Move, move!

299
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:28,500
You move!

300
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:42,040
You coward!

301
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:43,000
Come on, go!

302
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,373
Come on,

303
00:19:44,423 --> 00:19:48,220
Try harder!

304
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:52,220
S-senpai!

305
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:56,040
Idiot, right now I'm Masked Gambler!

306
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:58,840
Just hurry up and look at ringside!

307
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:00,140
Come on,

308
00:20:00,190 --> 00:20:03,340
Don't you dare slack off!

309
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:04,360
Hey,

310
00:20:06,740 --> 00:20:08,520
W-why is the Chief here?

311
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:11,160
We were supposed to keep
our identities secret!

312
00:20:11,300 --> 00:20:12,640
What do we do?!

313
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:15,300
If our identities get exposed,
we're in big trouble!

314
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:20,280
But we can't stop the
match halfway through either!

315
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:21,880
What should we do, Ryo-sama?!

316
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:27,560
If it comes to this, we have to make
sure no one finds out who we are!

317
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:31,720
Everyone, start the operation to
keep Chief Ohara from finding out!

318
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:57,900
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo...
No no no no no no no no no no no no!

319
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:58,500
Come on, that's it!

320
00:20:58,500 --> 00:20:59,320
Hey, hey!

321
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:00,980
Can't you see anything, hey!

322
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:02,180
There, there, there!

323
00:21:08,820 --> 00:21:11,660
I feel like I've seen those
wrestlers somewhere before.

324
00:21:11,660 --> 00:21:12,400
Customer,

325
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,820
you're Mr. Ohara, aren't you?

326
00:21:15,660 --> 00:21:16,680
Yes, that's me.

327
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:19,620
someone wishing to meet you has arrived,

328
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:23,040
so please come to Gate 131.

329
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:23,680
What?

330
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:25,720
But...

331
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:28,580
It can't be helped.

332
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:36,960
Good, now we're safe.

333
00:21:39,220 --> 00:21:41,280
Finally, number 72.

334
00:21:41,280 --> 00:21:44,680
Hurry, or the match will be over!

335
00:21:47,500 --> 00:21:50,020
The time has finally come to settle this.

336
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:53,160
I won't lose! That belt is mine!

337
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:04,920
It's a dead end.

338
00:22:04,920 --> 00:22:07,080
Gate 131 isn't here.

339
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:12,540
Come to think of it,
how did that attendant know my name?

340
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:14,160
We're in a real bind, we're in a real bind.

341
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:17,160
Who'd have thought
Chief Ohara would show up.

342
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:18,540
Seriously, seriously.

343
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:21,020
If he finds out we're doing pro wrestling,

344
00:22:21,020 --> 00:22:22,440
he's not going to let us off easy, is he?

345
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:23,100
You lot.

346
00:22:24,540 --> 00:22:25,260
Chief.

347
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,660
I've seen everything.

348
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:31,260
Now, you'd better explain yourselves.

349
00:22:32,580 --> 00:22:33,760
Aaaaaah!

350
00:22:33,760 --> 00:22:34,300
Aaaaaah!

351
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:35,580
Aaaaaah!

352
00:22:49,640 --> 00:22:50,800
We did it!

353
00:22:51,800 --> 00:23:01,000
We've become the first champions of the newly launched wrestling promotion!
The championship belt is about to be wrapped around the masked Gambler's waist.

354
00:23:01,460 --> 00:23:02,220
Wait a -

355
00:23:04,260 --> 00:23:07,500
Who wrote this?
I don't remember putting this in the script!

356
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:12,540
What a great plan! This Kitaba guy...

357
00:23:12,920 --> 00:23:13,240
Me?

358
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:14,580
I'm counting on you.

359
00:23:18,280 --> 00:23:19,260
Yaaah!

360
00:23:22,120 --> 00:23:23,820
I heard it from Terai-dashi!

361
00:23:24,360 --> 00:23:26,460
Dragging everyone into a wrestling show?!

362
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:28,700
You're probably the one behind this,

363
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:31,840
aren't you?
Promising yourself half the profits?

364
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:32,500
How about that!

365
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:35,100
This is charity work,

366
00:23:35,100 --> 00:23:38,200
but using your comrades to make money?
I won't stand for it!

367
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:40,200
I'll knock some sense into you, Ryotsu!

368
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:47,160
Give up! Give up! Give up!

369
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:48,820
What?

370
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:56,520
Unbelievable! A man who rushed in from the
audience has forced the champion to tap out!

371
00:23:57,020 --> 00:23:59,940
The second-generation champion
is a mysterious male spectator!

372
00:24:00,860 --> 00:24:01,880
What an idiot!

373
00:24:12,900 --> 00:24:18,660
Na na na na, na na na na, na na na na

374
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:24,260
for those who gamble
recklessly on their looks

375
00:24:24,260 --> 00:24:27,420
I probably don't want to become that

376
00:24:27,420 --> 00:24:32,040
if you're dawdling around the corner

377
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:34,340
the moon ran away

378
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:38,080
because now isn't everything

379
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:39,360
that crying voice from just now

380
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:42,580
don't get too worked up about it

381
00:24:42,580 --> 00:24:46,320
even if you fib or cheat a little

382
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:50,480
sometimes when you're helping someone

383
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:52,480
Baby, do you know me?

384
00:24:52,540 --> 00:24:56,840
Facing tomorrow with a nice spirit,

385
00:24:58,060 --> 00:25:01,840
don't get discouraged,
we'll do what we have to do.

386
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:04,300
Such a cute spirit.

387
00:25:04,300 --> 00:25:11,520
It's hard to tell because
that's how we want to seem.

388
00:25:11,520 --> 00:25:17,260
Isn't that better than a makeover?

389
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:32,280
My dream for the future
is a down-to-earth life.

390
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:35,140
Well, he's Terai's son,
so it can't be helped, right?

391
00:25:35,140 --> 00:25:39,380
After all, Terai's motto is
"Life's a treat-bunt."

392
00:25:39,380 --> 00:25:42,840
By the way, what does that
have to do with the stamp rally?

393
00:25:43,380 --> 00:25:47,040
Next time: Run, Terai!
A stamp rally for Father Terai!

394
00:25:47,260 --> 00:25:47,820
Thanks, see you!

